[Term]
id: ENVO:00000428
name: biome
def: "A biome is an ecosystem which is undergoing climactic ecological succession." [DOI:10.1186/2041-1480-4-43, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biome]
comment: In this definition, there is an assumption that no major perturbations are occurring or have occurred in a time frame affects the successional dynamics of the ecosystem. A "major" perturbation is one which disrupts the community's ability to restore its (near) equilibrium. Usually, pioneer or early secondary successional processes would be in effect in such scenarios.
synonym: "major habitat type" EXACT [WWF:Biome]
xref: EcoLexicon:biome
xref: LTER:809 {xref="https://vocab.lternet.edu/vocab/vocab/index.php?tema=809&/biomes"}
