[Term]
id: ExO:0000000
name: exposure stressor
def: "An agent, stimulus, activity, or event that causes stress or tension on an organism and interacts with an exposure_receptor during an exposure event." [CTD:curators]
is_a: BFO:0000040 ! material entity
relationship: interacts_with_an_exposure_receptor_via ExO:0000002 ! exposure event
relationship: RO:0002434 ExO:0000001 ! interacts with exposure recipient

[Term]
id: ExO:0000001
name: exposure recipient
def: "An entity (e.g., a human, human population, or a human organ) that interacts with an exposure stimulus during an exposure event." [CTD:curators]
synonym: "exposure receptor" EXACT []
synonym: "exposure target" EXACT []
is_a: BFO:0000040 ! material entity
relationship: RO:0002434 ExO:0000000 ! interacts with exposure stressor

[Term]
id: ExO:0000002
name: exposure event
def: "An interaction between an exposure stressor and an exposure_receptor." [CTD:curators]
is_a: BFO:0000015 ! process
relationship: BFO:0000051 ExO:0000000 ! has part exposure stressor
relationship: BFO:0000051 ExO:0000001 ! has part exposure recipient
relationship: interacts_with_an_exposure_receptor_via ExO:0000000 ! exposure stressor
relationship: interacts_with_an_exposure_stressor_via ExO:0000001 ! exposure recipient

[Term]
id: ExO:0000055
name: exposure route
def: "The way people, sample, or other living organisms come into contact with a stressor." [CTD:curators]
relationship: BFO:0000050 ExO:0000002 ! part of exposure event

[Term]
id: ExO:0000056
name: ingestion route
def: "An exposure route in which a subject or sample comes in contact with a stressor by swallowing the stressor or a substance containing the stressor." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153]
is_a: ExO:0000165 ! gastrointestinal tract route

[Term]
id: ExO:0000057
name: inhalation route
def: "An exposure route in which a subject or sample comes in contact with a stressor through breathing." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153]
is_a: ExO:0000055 ! exposure route

[Term]
id: ExO:0000060
name: injection route
def: "An exposure route in which a subject or sample comes in contact with a stressor that has directly entered the body through punctures, bites, or needles." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153]
is_a: ExO:0000055 ! exposure route

[Term]
id: ExO:0000159
name: maternal
def: "A route by which an exposure to a pregnant female causes an outcome in the fetus that might be observed long after birth" []
is_a: ExO:0000055 ! exposure route

[Term]
id: ExO:0000165
name: gastrointestinal tract route
def: "An exposure route in which a subject or sample comes in contact with a stressor in the subject's gastrointestinal tract." [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153]
is_a: ExO:0000055 ! exposure route

[Term]
id: FOODON:00001002
name: food product
def: "Food material for humans and animals which is processed with the intention that it be consumable as a whole or added to other food products." []
comment: The FoodOn "food product"class is provided as a branch under which new food product categories and food products themselves can be placed. Here classes are provided to differentiate a food product by its food composition, processing and/or consumption characteristics. This avoids brand name products but it may include generic food dish categories. It has a much greater depth and polyhierarchy than other agency product type schemes have in an effort to group related products together.  The upper level basis of this tree originated in the environment ontology (ENVO) and from the US Code of Federal Regulations.
is_a: FOODON:00002403 ! food material

[Term]
id: FOODON:00001006
name: mammalian meat food product
def: "A food product made of meat, the skeletal muscle and associated fat, and other edible tissues such as organs, livers, skin, brains, bone marrow, kidneys, or lungs, of mammals." []
xref: https://bioregistry.io/reference/siren\:F17332
is_a: FOODON:00001092 ! vertebrate food product
is_a: FOODON:00005501 ! mammal material
relationship: RO:0001000 FOODON:03411134 ! derives from mammal
relationship: RO:0002350 FOODON:03400150 ! member of meat or meat product (from mammal) (us cfr)

[Term]
id: FOODON:00001007
name: meat sausage food product
def: "A processed meat food product that is made from a sausage." []
is_a: FOODON:00001010 ! processed meat food product
relationship: RO:0002350 FOODON:03400221 ! member of sausage or luncheon meat (us cfr)

[Term]
id: FOODON:00001009
name: hot dog
def: "A hot dog is a moist sausage of soft, even texture and flavor, often made from advanced meat recovery or meat slurry. Most types are fully cooked, cured or smoked. It is often placed hot in a special purpose soft, sliced hot dog bun." []
synonym: "hotdog" EXACT []
is_a: FOODON:00001224 ! meat sausage (cooked)

[Term]
id: FOODON:00001010
name: processed meat food product
def: "A processed food product consisting of meat which has been subjected to preservation and/or taste altering processes such as grinding, salting, curing, fermentation, smoking, and addition of chemical preservatives." []
is_a: FOODON:00001006 ! mammalian meat food product
is_a: FOODON:03311737 ! processed food
relationship: FOODON:00001563 FOODON:02010113 ! has defining ingredient piece of animal meat (boneless)

[Term]
id: FOODON:00001011
name: milk formula food product
is_a: FOODON:00001091 ! dried milk food product
relationship: RO:0002350 FOODON:03400274 ! member of meal replacement (us cfr)

[Term]
id: FOODON:00001013
name: cheese food product
def: "Cheese is a food derived from milk that is produced in a wide range of flavors, textures, and forms by coagulation of the milk protein casein." []
synonym: "cheese" EXACT []
xref: https://bioregistry.io/reference/siren\:F1076
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheese
is_a: FOODON:00001256 ! dairy food product
relationship: FOODON:00001563 FOODON:03420245 ! has defining ingredient mammalian milk curd
relationship: RO:0002350 FOODON:03400115 ! member of cheese or cheese product (us cfr)

[Term]
id: FOODON:00001014
name: yogurt food product
def: "A dairy product produced by bacterial fermentation of milk." []
comment: The bacteria used to make yogurt are known as yogurt cultures. The fermentation of lactose by these bacteria produces lactic acid, which acts on milk protein to give yogurt its texture and characteristic tart flavor.
synonym: "yoghourt" EXACT []
synonym: "yoghurt" EXACT []
synonym: "yougert" EXACT []
is_a: FOODON:00001053 ! fermented dairy food product

[Term]
id: FOODON:00001015
name: plant food product
def: "A food product which has as a defining ingredient some plant material." []
is_a: FOODON:00001002 ! food product
is_a: FOODON:00004331 ! plant material

[Term]
id: FOODON:00001016
name: cabbage food product
def: "Cabbage or headed cabbage (comprising several cultivars of Brassica oleracea) is a leafy green or purple biennial plant, grown as an annual vegetable crop for its dense-leaved heads." []
xref: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabbage
is_a: FOODON:00001171 ! cruciferous inflorescence food product
is_a: FOODON:00003341 ! brassica food product
relationship: RO:0001000 NCBITaxon:3712 ! derives from Brassica oleracea

[Term]
id: FOODON:00001038
name: pork meat food product
def: "A food product made from domestic pig meat (Sus domesticus or Sus scrofa scrofa)." []
synonym: "pork" EXACT []
is_a: FOODON:00002663 ! pig food product
intersection_of: FOODON:00002663 ! pig food product
intersection_of: RO:0001000 FOODON:03302735 ! derives from pork meat (raw)
relationship: RO:0001000 FOODON:03302735 ! derives from pork meat (raw)

[Term]
id: FOODON:00001039
name: cured meat food product
def: "A meat that is preserved by the addition of a combination of salt, sugar, nitrates  or nitrite and or is smoked." [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cured_meat]
is_a: FOODON:00001010 ! processed meat food product
relationship: RO:0002350 FOODON:03400279 ! member of cured meat (us cfr)

[Term]
id: FOODON:00001040
name: chicken meat food product
def: "A food product that is derived from some chicken meat." []
is_a: FOODON:00001131 ! poultry meat food product
is_a: FOODON:02020149 ! chicken food product

[Term]
