[Term]
id: FOODON:03316764
name: vanilla bean extract
def: "Vanilla extract is a solution containing the flavor compound vanillin as the primary ingredient.  It is made by macerating and percolating vanilla pods in a solution of ethanol and water." []
comment: Wikipedia notes: Pure vanilla extract is made by macerating and percolating vanilla pods in a solution of ethanol and water. \n\nIn the United States, in order for a vanilla extract to be called pure, the U.S. Food and Drug Administration requires that the solution contains a minimum of 35% alcohol and 100 g of vanilla beans per litre (13.35 ounces per gallon).\n\nCanadian Regulations: Under the Food and Drug Regulations (C.R.C., c. 870), vanilla extract products have to be processed from vanilla beans: Vanilla planifolia or Vanilla tahitensia.
synonym: "natural vanilla" EXACT []
is_a: FOODON:00002328 ! vanilla bean food product
relationship: FOODON:00001301 FOODON:00002396 ! has food substance analog synthetic vanilla extract
