[Term]
id: FOODON:03411236
name: turkey (bird)
def: "The turkey is a large bird in the genus Meleagris, which is native to the Americas. Males of both turkey species have a distinctive fleshy wattle or protuberance that hangs from the top of the beak (called a snood). They are among the largest birds in their ranges. As in many galliformes, the male is larger and much more colorful than the female." []
xref: http://eol.org/pages/18523
