[Term]
id: FOODON:03411426
name: mackerel family
def: "The *Scombridae* family of the mackerels, tunas, and bonitos includes many of the most important and familiar food fishes. The family consists of 51 species in 15 genera and two subfamilies. All species are in the subfamily *Scombrinae*, except the butterfly kingfish, which is the sole member of subfamily *Gasterochismatinae*. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scombridae]" []
xref: http://eol.org/pages/5210
xref: langual:thesaurus.asp?termid=B1426
