[Term]
id: FOODON:03412112
name: mollusc
def: "Mollusca is a large phylum of invertebrate animals whose members are known as molluscs or mollusks. Molluscs are the largest marine phylum, comprising about 23% of all the named marine organisms. Numerous molluscs also live in freshwater and terrestrial habitats. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mollusca]" []
synonym: "Mollusca" EXACT []
synonym: "mollusk" EXACT []
xref: EC:No 216/2009 MOL
xref: http://eol.org/pages/2195
xref: https://www.fao.org/fishery/en/aqspecies/mol
xref: langual:thesaurus.asp?termid=B2112
