[Term]
id: FOODON:03420127
name: animal (whole or piece(s))
comment: This is from a LanguaL "ANIMAL BODY OR BODY PART" class. Its subclasses can be used if it is ambiguous what animal is being referred to, and whether the reference is being made to a whole animal or some part of it, including parts of organs.  However, see if a more precise term is available under either the "animal carcass" branch or the "piece of animal"branch.\n\nLanguaL curation note: Includes carcass meat, organ meat, and nonmeat parts of animals, as well as the whole animal.
xref: langual:thesaurus.asp?termid=C0127
