[Term]
id: FOODON:03430102
name: food (liquid, high viscosity)
def: "A liquid that flows slowly at room temperature." []
comment: Examples are: some heavy liqueurs, evaporated milk, vegetable oil, molasses and honey. The range of high viscosity liquids spans sucrose solutions between 45 and 70% solids (viscosity range from 10 to 500 centipoise). Prefer 'solid pieces' factor term to 'small particles' if both appear in the food.
xref: langual:thesaurus.asp?termid=E0102
