[Term]
id: FOODON:03430109
name: food (liquid, low viscosity)
def: "A liquid that flows very easily at room temperature." []
comment: Examples are: water, apple juice, sherry, acidophilus milk, whipping cream and some heavy liqueurs. The range of low viscosity liquid spans sucrose solutions between 0 and 45% solids (viscosity range from 1 to 10 centipoise). Prefer 'solid pieces' factor term to 'small particles' if both appear in the food.
xref: langual:thesaurus.asp?termid=E0109
